  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Isotorachrysone and the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, mediated through the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. Isotorachrysone is directly linked to this subunit, and Palmyramide A, which targets the same subunit, is also linked to the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. This indicates that Isotorachrysone may act through a common pathway involving the 26S proteasome subunit, which in turn influences the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. The scores from the two paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but the evidence is not definitive. The mechanism appears to involve the 26S proteasome subunit as a bridge between Isotorachrysone and the transporter, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction.",
